        <p class="Biblio"><a name="IEC60050-113" id="IEC60050-113"></a>[6]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>IEC 60050-113:2011, <i>International Electrotechnical Vocabulary (IEV) &#x2013; Part 113: Physics for electrotechnology</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="IEC60050-713" id="IEC60050-713"></a>[7]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>IEC 60050-713:1998, <i>International Electrotechnical Vocabulary (IEV) &#x2013; Part 713: Radiocommunications: transmitters, receivers, networks and operation</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="IEV" id="IEV"></a>[8]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>IEC Electropedia,
    <i>IEC Electropedia</i>
  </p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ITURTF460-6" id="ITURTF460-6"></a>[9]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ITU ITU-R TF.460-6,
    <i>Standard-frequency and time-signal emissions</i>
  </p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="BIPMRCCTF3" id="BIPMRCCTF3"></a>[10]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>BIPM Recommendation CCTF 3 (2017), Bureau International des Poids et Mesures / The International Bureau of Weights and Measures: Consultative Committee for Time and Frequency (CCTF),
<i>Report of the 21st meeting to the International Committee for Weights and Measures</i>, 2017</p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="IAUR24" id="IAUR24"></a>[11]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>International Astronomical Union Resolution B1.9 (2000), International Astronomical Union, <i>IAU Resolutions adopted at the 24th General Assembly</i>, 2000</p>
      </div>
      
    </div>
  <div style="mso-element:footnote-list"><div style="mso-element:footnote" id="ftn1">
  
